Subject: hookify: let the model see block reasons and warnings

Upstream hookify puts a rule's message only in systemMessage, which the human
sees and the model doesn't. A block returns a bare deny, so the model sees
just "Blocked by hook" and never learns the safe form, and a warn is invisible
to the model. Add permissionDecisionReason to the deny, and additionalContext
to PreToolUse/PostToolUse warnings.

Applied by ~/.claude/patches/bootstrap.sh to every installed hookify copy.

--- a/core/rule_engine.py	2026-10-10 20:46:44
+++ b/core/rule_engine.py	2026-10-10 20:47:18
@@ -73,7 +73,9 @@
                 return {
                     "hookSpecificOutput": {
                         "hookEventName": hook_event,
-                        "permissionDecision": "deny"
+                        "permissionDecision": "deny",
+                        # Shown to the model, so it sees why and the safe form.
+                        "permissionDecisionReason": combined_message
                     },
                     "systemMessage": combined_message
                 }
@@ -86,9 +88,15 @@
         # If only warnings, show them but allow operation
         if warning_rules:
             messages = [f"**[{r.name}]**\n{r.message}" for r in warning_rules]
-            return {
-                "systemMessage": "\n\n".join(messages)
-            }
+            combined_message = "\n\n".join(messages)
+            result = {"systemMessage": combined_message}
+            # systemMessage reaches only the human; additionalContext reaches the model.
+            if hook_event in ['PreToolUse', 'PostToolUse']:
+                result["hookSpecificOutput"] = {
+                    "hookEventName": hook_event,
+                    "additionalContext": combined_message
+                }
+            return result
 
         # No matches - allow operation
         return {}
